# SITL optical-flow + rangefinder setup — PHASE B (configure + point the EKF at flow).
#
# TARGET FIRMWARE: ArduCopter 4.6.x (the version our real FlywooF745 runs: 4.6.3).
# Values match ArduPilot's own Tools/autotest/default_params/copter-optflow.parm
# AT TAG Copter-4.6.3.
#
# !! PARAMETER NAMES ARE VERSION-SPECIFIC !!
#   4.5.x / 4.6.x : RNGFND1_MIN_CM / RNGFND1_MAX_CM   (centimetres)  <-- used here
#   4.7+ / master : RNGFND1_MIN    / RNGFND1_MAX      (metres)
# Loading the wrong variant silently skips those lines ("unknown parameter"), which
# leaves the rangefinder at its defaults — RNGFND1_MIN_CM defaults to 20 cm, and a
# sensor mounted a few cm above the floor then never reads "good", so the EKF gets no
# terrain height and arming fails with "Need Position Estimate".
#
# Load AFTER phase A + reboot (so the RNGFND1_* params exist), THEN REBOOT AGAIN
# (the analog rangefinder backend only picks up RNGFND1_PIN on the next boot):
#   param load /Users/danieleamore/Studium/Drohnen-mit-KI/Pi-Code/params/sitl_flow_phaseB.parm
#   reboot
#
# Note: we do NOT touch SIM_SONAR_SCALE — its default (12.1212) already matches
# RNGFND1_SCALING (12.12). And we do NOT disable GPS here: the EKF uses optical flow for
# horizontal position/velocity (POSXY=0, VELXY=OpticalFlow), while GPS still provides
# the origin/home so the geofence and "waiting for home" pre-arm are satisfied.
# For a truly GPS-denied run (Phase 3) load sitl_gps_off.parm afterwards.
# RNGFND1_PIN / RNGFND1_SCALING are deliberately absent: they only apply to the analog
# backend (RNGFND1_TYPE 1). Phase A selects type 100 (the simulator's own rangefinder),
# which needs no pin and no voltage scaling.
RNGFND1_MIN_CM 0
RNGFND1_MAX_CM 4000
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 0
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 5
EK3_SRC1_VELZ 0
# FuseAllVelocities off. Our flight controller uses 0 too (see the project docs); the
# firmware default is 1, which a wiped EEPROM restores.
EK3_SRC_OPTIONS 0
